        "encoding_method": "amplitude_encoding",
        "encoding_details": "Classical stock-price windows are encoded into quantum circuits; the paper states the circuit qubit count follows ceil(log2 b) + ceil(log2 f) + 1, where b and f are past and future window sizes. For the invertible FQGAN example, a past window of 16 and future window of 8 are used, and the generator outputs 16 future values with the first 8 overlapping the input.",
        "objective_function": "Minimize sum_{i=1}^{8} (a_i - f * y_hat_i)^2 to recover the normalization factor f, where a_i are min-max scaled overlapping input prices and y_hat_i are normalized predicted overlapping prices.",
